-- title:
--   Maximal ideals over mathfrak m_A are κ-rational points
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring whose residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A = A/\mathfrak m_A$ is algebraically closed, and let $C$ be a commutative $A$-algebra that is of finite type over $A$ (a quotient of a polynomial ring in finitely many variables over $A$). Let $y \subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ such that the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A$ under the structure map $A \to C$ is contained in $y$, i.e. $y$ lies over $\mathfrak m_A$. The assertion is that there exists an $A$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : C \to \kappa$ whose kernel, as a ring homomorphism, is exactly $y$. The two types $A$ and $C$ are allowed to live in different universes. No uniqueness is claimed, although the map is in fact unique.
--
--   This is the statement that a closed point of the special fibre of a finite-type scheme over a local ring with algebraically closed residue field is rational over that residue field; it is the form of the Nullstellensatz used to produce $\kappa$-points from maximal ideals. It is invoked in the project when closed points of special fibres must be realised as $\kappa$-valued algebra homomorphisms, for instance in the analysis of divisors on polarised schemes and in the chart-level study of modular curves in characteristic $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_algHom_residueField_ker_eq_of_isMaximal_of_finiteType.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open IsLocalRing

theorem IsLocalRing.exists_algHom_residueField_ker_eq_of_isMaximal_of_finiteType
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsAlgClosed (ResidueField A)]
    {C : Type v} [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] [Algebra.FiniteType A C]
    (y : Ideal C) [y.IsMaximal] (hy : (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A C) ≤ y) :
    ∃ ψ : C →ₐ[A] ResidueField A, RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom = y := by sorry
